# Gauntlet's run artifacts: events.jsonl, stop-attempts.json, junit.xml and coverage.json.
# The event log is the authority on a verdict and lives here, uncommitted; `gauntlet check
# --record PATH` writes a run's record to a path a repository can carry, never here.
.gauntlet/
# mutmut's working copy of the source tree; left behind, it collides with pytest collection.
mutants/
# mutmut's cache.
.mutmut-cache
# pytest-cov's data file, written at the project root by the tests gate's --cov.
.coverage
# Written by no gate — the tests gate's JSON report goes to .gauntlet/coverage.json.
# A hand-run `pytest --cov-report=json` lands here.
coverage.json
# Tool caches.
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
# Not produced by this project's build backend (hatchling); a setuptools-style install would.
*.egg-info/
# Emacs: backup files, auto-save files, and lock files. A lock file is a dangling symlink,
# which mutmut's tree copy dies on; gates/mutation.py names it in the remedy.
*~
\#*\#
.\#*
